Q2. Circular Queue Using Array
Definition:
Circular Queue ek queue hai jisme last position ke baad next position first position hoti hai. Isse array ki unused positions ko dobara use kiya ja sakta hai.
Required operations: ENQUEUE, DEQUEUE, FRONT, DISPLAY. Queue ko properly full aur empty distinguish karna chahiye. DSA Assignment Structures & Algorithms.docx
C Program
#include <stdio.h>

#define MAX 5

int queue[MAX];
int front = -1;
int rear = -1;

// ENQUEUE operation
void enqueue(int x)
{
    if ((rear + 1) % MAX == front)
    {
        printf("Queue is Full!\n");
    }
    else
    {
        if (front == -1)
        {
            front = 0;
        }

        rear = (rear + 1) % MAX;
        queue[rear] = x;

        printf("%d inserted into queue.\n", x);
    }
}

// DEQUEUE operation
void dequeue()
{
    if (front == -1)
    {
        printf("Queue is Empty!\n");
    }
    else
    {
        printf("%d deleted from queue.\n", queue[front]);

        if (front == rear)
        {
            front = -1;
            rear = -1;
        }
        else
        {
            front = (front + 1) % MAX;
        }
    }
}

// FRONT operation
void showFront()
{
    if (front == -1)
    {
        printf("Queue is Empty!\n");
    }
    else
    {
        printf("Front element = %d\n", queue[front]);
    }
}

// DISPLAY operation
void display()
{
    if (front == -1)
    {
        printf("Queue is Empty!\n");
    }
    else
    {
        int i = front;

        printf("Queue elements are:\n");

        while (1)
        {
            printf("%d ", queue[i]);

            if (i == rear)
                break;

            i = (i + 1) % MAX;
        }

        printf("\n");
    }
}

int main()
{
    int choice, value;

    while (1)
    {
        printf("\n--- CIRCULAR QUEUE MENU ---\n");
        printf("1. ENQUEUE\n");
        printf("2. DEQUEUE\n");
        printf("3. FRONT\n");
        printf("4. DISPLAY\n");
        printf("5. EXIT\n");

        printf("Enter your choice: ");
        scanf("%d", &choice);

        switch (choice)
        {
            case 1:
                printf("Enter value: ");
                scanf("%d", &value);
                enqueue(value);
                break;

            case 2:
                dequeue();
                break;

            case 3:
                showFront();
                break;

            case 4:
                display();
                break;

            case 5:
                return 0;

            default:
                printf("Invalid choice!\n");
        }
    }
}
Circular Queue vs Linear Queue
1. Better memory utilization:
Circular queue mein rear last index par pahunchne ke baad beginning ki unused positions ko reuse kar sakta hai. Isliye memory ka better utilization hota hai. DSA Assignment Structures & Algorithms.docx
2. Time Complexity:
ENQUEUE = O(1)
DEQUEUE = O(1) DSA Assignment Structures & Algorithms.docx
3. Space Complexity:
Circular Queue = O(n), jahan n queue ki capacity hai. DSA Assignment Structures & Algorithms.docx
4. Linear Queue ki problem:
Linear queue mein agar REAR last index tak pahunch jata hai, to beginning mein kuch positions empty hone ke baad bhi new element insert nahi kiya ja sakta. Is problem ko circular queue solve karta hai. DSA Assignment Structures & Algorithms.docx
